>   happened to Voltron with the WoW at the castle.  It only had 2 charges;
>   she realized this only after zapping it the third time. (argh!)

	Based upon personal experience, I'd say >1%.  Bum deal.

>3. [this question has come up before (sorry)]
>   Voltron has been appointed by her god Odin as the 'Envoy of Balance'.
>   What does this mean, and what are the advantages to her?

	Every alignment has its own special avatar, for the Neutrals it's the
Envoy of Balance.  Being named an avatar means you get some nifty intrinsics
(I don't recall which ones), a nice sword, and your prayer timeout is roughly
tripled.  Although it sounds nifty, I normally try to avoid it since by the
time I get it, I already have a good weapon and most of the intrinsics I need.
The extended prayer timeout I could really do without.

